WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.020
Good Morning John!

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.700
It's very nearly Christmas,

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.540
and so Katherine and I have come together to answer people's Christmas Questions.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.520
We like Christmas!

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.620
I guess we do, yeah. I mean...

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.620
Taha wants to know:

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.820
"Is it like the films? I've never experienced Christmas day with people who celebrate Christmas."

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.280
You mean like Die Hard? 'Cause it's exactly like Die Hard.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.420
Got invited to the Christmas party by mistake.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.780
What's another good Christmas movie?

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.040
It's a Wonderful Life.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.140
Well...

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.620
I haven't seen that one.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:27.220
What!?

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.180
- I'll give you the moon Mary.
- I'll take it.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.780
I've seen parts of it, I've never watched the whole thing.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:36.780
I got the sense that it was a real downer and that's not what I want at Christmas!

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.900
I mean there's, like, feasts, and there's opening presents, and there's stockings.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.000
All the tropes are there. You eat spaghetti with maple syrup.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.980
Katherine: And cotton balls.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.080
"Whose idea was it to bring a tree inside and then decorate it?"

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.080
-Oh, Germans?
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.660
- Well, around that area.
-Well, yeah...
- 'Cause Germany didn't exist.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:58.840
- Right right right, but like, the Germanic... folks.
- I think the idea was it's the middle of winter,

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.800
and we're depressed, so we need some green up in here!

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.340
Spring's a long time away.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.260
I was reading that they would hang trees from the ceiling.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:09.860
- Right, well, you know the house is small so you probably couldn't...
- Right.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.920
- ...didn't have a lot of floor space, to like...
- Ah, good point.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.920
Before they had the trees and also people who couldn't afford a full tree would just have, like, pine boughs.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.020
- Oh, like the Christmas branch?
- And it smells good. Yeah.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.320
Emmet Otter's Christmas branch!

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.080
Katherine has a real love affair with 'Emmet Otter's Jug-Band Christmas'.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.420
Emmet Otter: At least there ain't no hole in the washtub.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.120
We are talking about it now which means Katherine's going to cry for a while. We'll be back in a little bit.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:38.180
- I'm better. The thing that I have a problem with Christmas is that it comes, it's done, it's over. Bye-bye.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.580
And then you're like: 'Huh, wha-, whe-?'

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:44.040
- Yeah, we did all, we were prepped for so long!
- I got all this stuff happening in my house now.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.700
- What I gotta do? Just put it away?
- Christmas...

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.840
- No, I leave it up for...
- Christmas ends...

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.000
...pretty much most of January.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.300
...when you can blow on the tree and the needles fall off.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.380
Oh gosh, that's too late.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.140
It's really dangerous actually, you shouldn't do that.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.040
Have you ever seen a Christmas tree fire? There's lots of Youtube videos, in fact, I'll put one right here, right now.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.120
I didn't like it.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.620
"Where do I get last-minute Christmas presents?"

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.360
What do you got in your cupboards? Didn't use that soap yet.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.560
- Here's some Irish Spring.
- Yeah.
- Carve it with a knife.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.040
Look, in these green and white stripes are two deodorants to get a man fresh and clean.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.720
Did you know that Turtles All the Way Down was named a best book of the year by

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.300
The New York Times, The Wall Street Journal, Entertainment Weekly, Time Magazine,

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:26.640
NPR, Buzzfeed, Amazon, Barnes &amp; Noble, The Onion, The A.V. Club, Publishers Weekly and Booklist

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.320
And it's available at a bookstore near you!

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.080
- That's a lot of lists, John.
- That's a lot of lists!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.580
- Congratulations. Um, yeah.
- That's like, all the lists!

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.120
- Yes.
- Are there any more lists?!

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.700
"What do people in summer climates do for Christmas?" Same stuff.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.620
Yeah, I mean, without the sweaters probably.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.720
"Why is it traditional to have a fruitcake?" Because the world is terrible.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.460
I think it was special to have fruit at this time of year.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.240
Where does the fruit come from?

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:55.360
Oh, it's dried. You put a bunch of booze in it. That's your mince.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:56.220
Mince!

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.760
You feed me mince!?

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.660
- And it's like being able to eat a fruit in the middle of winter. 
- Yeah.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:05.440
It's not... exactly like it, but it's reminiscent.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.400
Close as you can get.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.480
"What do Americans do on Boxing Day? What do you call that?"

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:12.600
-We call it the day after Christmas and we go back to work.
-It's not a thing.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:16.320
You bring the boxes out, you put all your Christmas decorations in them, and that's Boxing Day.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.700
"What's the deal with the pickle?"

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:23.440
Do you know what the deal with the pickle is? 'Cause several people asked about the pickle.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.400
Are they messing with us?

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.540
Is there a Christmas pickle?

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.760
Is this like Gigi the Christmas snake?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.480
Kids: Gigi!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.900
Thank you for your questions. Thank you, Katherine for being here.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:41.520
Anytime. Not really. This is a once a year thing!

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.060
John, we'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.280
Banging on the table, demanding figgy pudding.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.520
- They're wassailing you, asking... 
- Wassailing all over the town.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.300
Eating fruit and getting drunk.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.660
You wassailed at the Wenceslas estate?

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:57.560
What, how is it RE-fridgerator? Why aren't they just called fridgerators?

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.704
Happy Christmas.

